spec: specs/di.md (new), stage 0

why: provide/providing/wire make a dependency a type and a missing one a
  compile error, but an installer holds a READY value: nothing opens a
  pool, orders start/stop, or lets one module's acquisition see the
  module before it. That is the gap between "context functions" and DI.

what: type Module[F] = Providing[F] ! Resource in the core; module(acquire)(release),
  Module.value, Module(providing), `and` whose right operand is F[Module[G]]
  so a dependent module reads its dependency with wire[..], apply(body)
  into Resource.run. Tests: order/reverse release, dependent module, test
  override, missing dependency is a compile error. Spec first, then the
  stages for qualifiers, printed plan, okay-spring/ZLayer bridges.

